---
import SiteLayout from '../layouts/SiteLayout.astro';
import ImageToolGrid from '../components/ImageToolGrid.astro';
---
<SiteLayout title="Free Online Image Tools — Batch Resize, Compress, Crop & More | ConvertAnyFile" description="Private browser-based image tools for resizing, compressing, rotating, cropping, blurring and visible-watermark editing. Batch up to 50 images with shared or per-image settings.">
<section class="page-hero"><div class="site-container hero-inner"><div class="breadcrumbs"><a href="/">Home</a><span>/</span><span>Image Tools</span></div><span class="eyebrow">Free Online Image Tools</span><h1>Private image edits that run in your browser.</h1><p>Resize, compress, rotate, crop, blur or repair visible watermarks without sending source images to an image-processing API. Batch tools share one queue and let you switch between one setup for all images and per-image overrides.</p></div></section>
<section class="content-wide-section"><div class="site-container"><div class="section-heading wide"><span class="section-kicker">Image Tools</span><h2>Choose a focused tool, then keep the same batch workflow.</h2><p>Resize, Compress, Rotate / Flip, Crop and Blur are available as preview tools on the shared Image Tools platform. Remove Watermark and Gemini Watermark Remover continue to use the mask editor on the same platform foundation.</p></div><ImageToolGrid /></div></section>
<section class="content-wide-section white"><div class="site-container"><div class="content-intro-grid"><div><span class="section-kicker">Shared or individual</span><h2>Apply one setup to the batch, or customize exceptions.</h2><p>Start in Apply to all for repeated work. Switch to Edit individually when a specific image needs different dimensions, compression quality, orientation, crop coordinates or blur region. Custom settings stay attached to that image while the rest continue inheriting shared settings.</p></div><div class="content-summary-card"><strong>Local by design</strong><p>Image decoding, live preview, processing, output encoding and ZIP creation happen in your browser. Processing is sequential so large batches do not need every full-resolution image in memory at once.</p></div></div></div></section>
<section class="content-wide-section"><div class="site-container"><div class="section-heading wide"><span class="section-kicker">Phase 3 preview</span><h2>Five deterministic tools now share one platform.</h2><p>Resize supports pixels, percentage and fit-to-box. Compress supports per-image format and quality. Rotate / Flip handles orientation changes. Crop uses normalized coordinates and common ratios. Blur supports the whole image or a manual rectangular region.</p></div><div class="callout"><strong>Still planned</strong><p>Remove Object and Remove Background remain separate roadmap items because they require more advanced editing or segmentation engines.</p></div></div></section>
</SiteLayout>
